flatpkg needs two things configured before it can launch anything:

  1. The store.  It is a real OSTree repo driven by the native ostree
     binary (sysutils/libostree).

  2. The daemon, which is the only privileged component:
       sysrc flatpkgd_enable=YES

A group member may use the daemon.  To join it:
  pw groupadd flatpkg && pw groupmod flatpkg -m <user>

Note that a jail is only as good as its kernel modules.  If every flatpkg
command reports a missing module, load the ones the store and the sandbox
need, in rc.conf:
  linux64_load="YES"
  nullfs_load="YES"
  linprocfs_load="YES"
  linsysfs_load="YES"
  unionfs_load="YES"
  fdescfs_load="YES"
